WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.427
Your phone has a passcode, and your photos may be backed up to the cloud. A business protects its accounting records on computer in the same kinds of way.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:24.164
Data is at risk in two main ways. It can be lost or damaged. Or it can be seen or changed by people who should not have access. That is called unauthorised access.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:32.433
Step one. Decide what the question is about: stopping access, stopping loss, or both.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:44.508
Step two. To stop access, use passwords, a firewall, anti-virus software, encryption, or locked rooms. To stop loss, take regular backups and keep copies off-site or in the cloud.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:53.645
Step three. Write one different measure for each mark, in a few words. No long explanation is needed for a state question.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:01:07.001
Here is a real question from November 2025, Paper 1. State three ways that data may be protected when using a computerised accounting system. Three marks.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:13.059
First, stop outsiders getting in through the internet. Install a firewall.

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:19.783
Second, stop harmful programs damaging or stealing data. Use anti-virus software.

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:34.213
Third, stop unauthorised people using the system. Protect it with strong passwords. Check: three different ideas. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:46.083
A common mistake is giving the same method twice in different words. Passwords and secret login codes are one idea, so they earn one mark.

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:54.425
Another is writing something vague, such as keep it safe, or giving a benefit of computers instead. Name a specific measure.

00:01:55.550 --> 00:02:09.419
Now you try. Lena runs a travel agency. Read her problems, then state one way to protect her data from each risk. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:23.255
The staff problem is access, so protect the accounts with a strong password. The hard drive problem is loss, so back up the data regularly and keep a copy off-site or in the cloud.

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:32.609
Remember: decide the risk, choose a matching measure, and give one different idea for each mark. Now try the practice questions.
